{"call_id":"call_Wc9v4NeFk8mVm07jfKvkFgl3","process_id":"63674","turn_id":"019ca6f3-bdcd-7df2-b6dc-7bf429771b5e","command":["/usr/bin/bash","-lc","kspec meta get @task-work-loop --json"],"cwd":"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"kspec meta get @task-work-loop --json"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","stdout":"{\n  \"_ulid\": \"01KJKBFYG5K4XTGZJGXRFMP1YD\",\n  \"id\": \"task-work-loop\",\n  \"trigger\": \"manual\",\n  \"description\": \"Loop variant of task-work-session for autonomous agents. Auto-filters to automation-eligible tasks, auto-resolves decisions. Task selection: needs_work > in_progress > unblocking > priority. Includes local-review subagent step and fix cycle handling for needs_work tasks. Verifies work needed including trait AC coverage. Implementation quality: search for existing utilities, match code style, run full test suite. PR review handled externally by ralph.\",\n  \"steps\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": \"action\",\n      \"content\": \"Filter to automation-eligible tasks only.\\nUse: kspec tasks ready --eligible\\nThis ensures only tasks marked automation: eligible are considered.\\n\",\n      \"execution\": {\n        \"mode\": \"silent\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"decision\",\n      \"content\": \"Select task by priority order.\\nFirst, run `kspec tasks ready --eligible` — its output is authoritative. Do not select exit based on assumptions.\\nCheck in order:\\n1. needs_work tasks (fix cycle — address review feedback, highest priority)\\n2. in_progress tasks (continue existing work)\\n3. Ready tasks that unblock others (high impact)\\n4. Highest priority ready task (lowest number = higher priority)\\n\\nNote: pending_review tasks are handled externally by ralph spawning PR review subagents.\\n\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"needs_work task exists -> fix review feedback (fix cycle)\",\n        \"in_progress task exists -> continue that task\",\n        \"Ready task unblocks others -> select that task\",\n        \"Only isolated ready tasks -> select highest priority (lowest number)\",\n        \"`kspec tasks ready --eligible` returned empty -> stop responding (ralph exits automatically)\",\n        \"`kspec tasks ready --eligible` shows all blocked -> stop responding (ralph exits automatically)\"\n      ],\n      \"execution\": {\n        \"mode\": \"silent\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"check\",\n      \"content\": \"Verify work is needed - but VALIDATE, don't trust notes.\\n\\nNotes are context, not proof. If a task is in the queue, there's a reason.\\n\\nTo mark \\\"Already implemented\\\" you MUST:\\n1. RUN the tests (npm test) - they must PASS, not skip\\n2. VERIFY own AC coverage - each spec AC has a test annotated // AC: @spec-ref ac-N\\n3. VERIFY trait AC coverage - each inherited trait AC has a test annotated // AC: @trait-slug ac-N\\n4. RUN kspec validate - zero trait AC coverage warnings for your spec\\n5. CHECK implementation matches spec requirements\\n\\nDO NOT mark complete just because:\\n- Notes say \\\"already done\\\" (verify yourself)\\n- Tests exist but skip in CI (that's a gap to fix)\\n- Someone said it was implemented (run the tests)\\n\\nTreat this like a code review - validate the actual work.\\n\",\n      \"on_fail\": \"Only if tests PASS and ACs are COVERED:\\nMark task complete with \\\"Already implemented\\\" reason and EXIT\\n\",\n      \"execution\": {\n        \"mode\": \"silent\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"action\",\n      \"content\": \"Start selected task (if not already in_progress).\\nUse: kspec task start @task\\n\\nIf task has plan_ref, load plan context before deep implementation work:\\n  1. Check task link: kspec task get @task\\n  2. If plan_ref is non-null: kspec plan get @plan-ref\\n\",\n      \"execution\": {\n        \"mode\": \"silent\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"action\",\n      \"content\": \"Work on the task, adding notes as you go.\\nUse: kspec task note @task \\\"What you're doing...\\\"\\nAdd notes during work, not just at end.\\n\\nSCOPE EXPANSION: If you discover missing implementation while testing,\\nimplementing it IS in scope. The goal is verified behavior, not just test files.\\n\\\"Add tests for X\\\" means \\\"ensure X is verified\\\" - if X doesn't exist, implement it.\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"check\",\n      \"content\": \"Verify Definition of Done before committing.\\n\\nRead task notes for any DoD criteria. Common constraints:\\n- \\\"No test.skip() calls\\\" - verify no skipped tests in changes\\n- \\\"All own ACs covered\\\" - verify each spec AC has corresponding test\\n- \\\"All trait ACs covered\\\" - verify each inherited trait AC has test\\n- \\\"No TODO/FIXME\\\" - no placeholder comments\\n- \\\"No duplicated logic\\\" - search for existing utilities before writing new code\\n\\nCRITICAL: Never use test.skip() to document missing functionality.\\nIf functionality is missing, implement it - that's in scope.\\n\\nIf DoD criteria exist and are not met, fix the gaps first.\\n\",\n      \"on_fail\": \"Do not proceed with DoD violations.\\nEither fix the gaps or escalate to user if scope is unclear.\\n\",\n      \"execution\": {\n        \"mode\": \"silent\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"action\",\n      \"content\": \"Commit changes with Task: @task trailer.\\nAll changes must be committed before submitting.\\n\",\n      \"execution\": {\n        \"mode\": \"silent\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"action\",\n      \"content\": \"Run local review via subagent before submitting.\\nSpawn a subagent using Task tool with prompt:\\n\\\"Run /local-review for @spec-ref. Report all findings with severity.\\\"\\n\\nIf MUST-FIX findings: fix them, re-commit, re-run local review.\\nIf SHOULD-FIX or SUGGESTION only: note findings, proceed to submit.\\nIf actionable items not worth fixing now: kspec inbox add \\\"...\\\"\\n\",\n      \"execution\": {\n        \"mode\": \"silent\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"action\",\n      \"content\": \"If this is a fix cycle (needs_work task):\\n  1. Read PR review comments: gh api repos/{owner}/{repo}/pulls/{number}/reviews\\n  2. Fix MUST-FIX and SHOULD-FIX issues identified in comments\\n  3. Commit and push fixes to PR branch\\n  4. Submit task: kspec task submit @task\\n  5. Stop responding — reviewer re-reviews in next iteration\\n\\nOtherwise (new work):\\n  1. Submit task: kspec task submit @task\\n  2. Create PR: /pr skill\\n  3. Stop responding — ralph handles PR review via separate subagent\\n\",\n      \"execution\": {\n        \"mode\": \"silent\"\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"_sourceFile\": \"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/.kspec/kynetic.meta.yaml\"\n}\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"_ulid\": \"01KJKBFYG5K4XTGZJGXRFMP1YD\",\n  \"id\": \"task-work-loop\",\n  \"trigger\": \"manual\",\n  \"description\": \"Loop variant of task-work-session for autonomous agents. Auto-filters to automation-eligible tasks, auto-resolves decisions. Task selection: needs_work > in_progress > unblocking > priority. Includes local-review subagent step and fix cycle handling for needs_work tasks. Verifies work needed including trait AC coverage. Implementation quality: search for existing utilities, match code style, run full test suite. PR review handled externally by ralph.\",\n  \"steps\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": \"action\",\n      \"content\": \"Filter to automation-eligible tasks only.\\nUse: kspec tasks ready --eligible\\nThis ensures only tasks marked automation: eligible are considered.\\n\",\n      \"execution\": {\n        \"mode\": \"silent\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"decision\",\n      \"content\": \"Select task by priority order.\\nFirst, run `kspec tasks ready --eligible` — its output is authoritative. Do not select exit based on assumptions.\\nCheck in order:\\n1. needs_work tasks (fix cycle — address review feedback, highest priority)\\n2. in_progress tasks (continue existing work)\\n3. Ready tasks that unblock others (high impact)\\n4. Highest priority ready task (lowest number = higher priority)\\n\\nNote: pending_review tasks are handled externally by ralph spawning PR review subagents.\\n\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"needs_work task exists -> fix review feedback (fix cycle)\",\n        \"in_progress task exists -> continue that task\",\n        \"Ready task unblocks others -> select that task\",\n        \"Only isolated ready tasks -> select highest priority (lowest number)\",\n        \"`kspec tasks ready --eligible` returned empty -> stop responding (ralph exits automatically)\",\n        \"`kspec tasks ready --eligible` shows all blocked -> stop responding (ralph exits automatically)\"\n      ],\n      \"execution\": {\n        \"mode\": \"silent\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"check\",\n      \"content\": \"Verify work is needed - but VALIDATE, don't trust notes.\\n\\nNotes are context, not proof. If a task is in the queue, there's a reason.\\n\\nTo mark \\\"Already implemented\\\" you MUST:\\n1. RUN the tests (npm test) - they must PASS, not skip\\n2. VERIFY own AC coverage - each spec AC has a test annotated // AC: @spec-ref ac-N\\n3. VERIFY trait AC coverage - each inherited trait AC has a test annotated // AC: @trait-slug ac-N\\n4. RUN kspec validate - zero trait AC coverage warnings for your spec\\n5. CHECK implementation matches spec requirements\\n\\nDO NOT mark complete just because:\\n- Notes say \\\"already done\\\" (verify yourself)\\n- Tests exist but skip in CI (that's a gap to fix)\\n- Someone said it was implemented (run the tests)\\n\\nTreat this like a code review - validate the actual work.\\n\",\n      \"on_fail\": \"Only if tests PASS and ACs are COVERED:\\nMark task complete with \\\"Already implemented\\\" reason and EXIT\\n\",\n      \"execution\": {\n        \"mode\": \"silent\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"action\",\n      \"content\": \"Start selected task (if not already in_progress).\\nUse: kspec task start @task\\n\\nIf task has plan_ref, load plan context before deep implementation work:\\n  1. Check task link: kspec task get @task\\n  2. If plan_ref is non-null: kspec plan get @plan-ref\\n\",\n      \"execution\": {\n        \"mode\": \"silent\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"action\",\n      \"content\": \"Work on the task, adding notes as you go.\\nUse: kspec task note @task \\\"What you're doing...\\\"\\nAdd notes during work, not just at end.\\n\\nSCOPE EXPANSION: If you discover missing implementation while testing,\\nimplementing it IS in scope. The goal is verified behavior, not just test files.\\n\\\"Add tests for X\\\" means \\\"ensure X is verified\\\" - if X doesn't exist, implement it.\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"check\",\n      \"content\": \"Verify Definition of Done before committing.\\n\\nRead task notes for any DoD criteria. Common constraints:\\n- \\\"No test.skip() calls\\\" - verify no skipped tests in changes\\n- \\\"All own ACs covered\\\" - verify each spec AC has corresponding test\\n- \\\"All trait ACs covered\\\" - verify each inherited trait AC has test\\n- \\\"No TODO/FIXME\\\" - no placeholder comments\\n- \\\"No duplicated logic\\\" - search for existing utilities before writing new code\\n\\nCRITICAL: Never use test.skip() to document missing functionality.\\nIf functionality is missing, implement it - that's in scope.\\n\\nIf DoD criteria exist and are not met, fix the gaps first.\\n\",\n      \"on_fail\": \"Do not proceed with DoD violations.\\nEither fix the gaps or escalate to user if scope is unclear.\\n\",\n      \"execution\": {\n        \"mode\": \"silent\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"action\",\n      \"content\": \"Commit changes with Task: @task trailer.\\nAll changes must be committed before submitting.\\n\",\n      \"execution\": {\n        \"mode\": \"silent\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"action\",\n      \"content\": \"Run local review via subagent before submitting.\\nSpawn a subagent using Task tool with prompt:\\n\\\"Run /local-review for @spec-ref. Report all findings with severity.\\\"\\n\\nIf MUST-FIX findings: fix them, re-commit, re-run local review.\\nIf SHOULD-FIX or SUGGESTION only: note findings, proceed to submit.\\nIf actionable items not worth fixing now: kspec inbox add \\\"...\\\"\\n\",\n      \"execution\": {\n        \"mode\": \"silent\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"action\",\n      \"content\": \"If this is a fix cycle (needs_work task):\\n  1. Read PR review comments: gh api repos/{owner}/{repo}/pulls/{number}/reviews\\n  2. Fix MUST-FIX and SHOULD-FIX issues identified in comments\\n  3. Commit and push fixes to PR branch\\n  4. Submit task: kspec task submit @task\\n  5. Stop responding — reviewer re-reviews in next iteration\\n\\nOtherwise (new work):\\n  1. Submit task: kspec task submit @task\\n  2. Create PR: /pr skill\\n  3. Stop responding — ralph handles PR review via separate subagent\\n\",\n      \"execution\": {\n        \"mode\": \"silent\"\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"_sourceFile\": \"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/.kspec/kynetic.meta.yaml\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":221487366},"formatted_output":"{\n  \"_ulid\": \"01KJKBFYG5K4XTGZJGXRFMP1YD\",\n  \"id\": \"task-work-loop\",\n  \"trigger\": \"manual\",\n  \"description\": \"Loop variant of task-work-session for autonomous agents. Auto-filters to automation-eligible tasks, auto-resolves decisions. Task selection: needs_work > in_progress > unblocking > priority. Includes local-review subagent step and fix cycle handling for needs_work tasks. Verifies work needed including trait AC coverage. Implementation quality: search for existing utilities, match code style, run full test suite. PR review handled externally by ralph.\",\n  \"steps\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": \"action\",\n      \"content\": \"Filter to automation-eligible tasks on