se:\\n- Notes say \\\"already done\\\" (verify yourself)\\n- Tests exist but skip in CI (that's a gap to fix)\\n- Someone said it was implemented (run the tests)\\n\\nTreat this like a code review - validate the actual work.\\n\",\n      \"on_fail\": \"Only if tests PASS and ACs are COVERED:\\nMark task complete with \\\"Already implemented\\\" reason and EXIT\\n\",\n      \"execution\": {\n        \"mode\": \"silent\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"action\",\n      \"content\": \"Start selected task (if not already in_progress).\\nUse: kspec task start @task\\n\\nIf task has plan_ref, load plan context before deep implementation work:\\n  1. Check task link: kspec task get @task\\n  2. If plan_ref is non-null: kspec plan get @plan-ref\\n\",\n      \"execution\": {\n        \"mode\": \"silent\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"action\",\n      \"content\": \"Work on the task, adding notes as you go.\\nUse: kspec task note @task \\\"What you're doing...\\\"\\nAdd notes during work, not just at end.\\n\\nSCOPE EXPANSION: If you discover missing implementation while testing,\\nimplementing it IS in scope. The goal is verified behavior, not just test files.\\n\\\"Add tests for X\\\" means \\\"ensure X is verified\\\" - if X doesn't exist, implement it.\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"check\",\n      \"content\": \"Verify Definition of Done before committing.\\n\\nRead task notes for any DoD criteria. Common constraints:\\n- \\\"No test.skip() calls\\\" - verify no skipped tests in changes\\n- \\\"All own ACs covered\\\" - verify each spec AC has corresponding test\\n- \\\"All trait ACs covered\\\" - verify each inherited trait AC has test\\n- \\\"No TODO/FIXME\\\" - no placeholder comments\\n- \\\"No duplicated logic\\\" - search for existing utilities before writing new code\\n\\nCRITICAL: Never use test.skip() to document missing functionality.\\nIf functionality is missing, implement it - that's in scope.\\n\\nIf DoD criteria exist and are not met, fix the gaps first.\\n\",\n      \"on_fail\": \"Do not proceed with DoD violations.\\nEither fix the gaps or escalate to user if scope is unclear.\\n\",\n      \"execution\": {\n        \"mode\": \"silent\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"action\",\n      \"content\": \"Commit changes with Task: @task trailer.\\nAll changes must be committed before submitting.\\n\",\n      \"execution\": {\n        \"mode\": \"silent\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"action\",\n      \"content\": \"Run local review via subagent before submitting.\\nSpawn a subagent using Task tool with prompt:\\n\\\"Run /local-review for @spec-ref. Report all findings with severity.\\\"\\n\\nIf MUST-FIX findings: fix them, re-commit, re-run local review.\\nIf SHOULD-FIX or SUGGESTION only: note findings, proceed to submit.\\nIf actionable items not worth fixing now: kspec inbox add \\\"...\\\"\\n\",\n      \"execution\": {\n        \"mode\": \"silent\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"action\",\n      \"content\": \"If this is a fix cycle (needs_work task):\\n  1. Read PR review comments: gh api repos/{owner}/{repo}/pulls/{number}/reviews\\n  2. Fix MUST-FIX and SHOULD-FIX issues identified in comments\\n  3. Commit and push fixes to PR branch\\n  4. Submit task: kspec task submit @task\\n  5. Stop responding — reviewer re-reviews in next iteration\\n\\nOtherwise (new work):\\n  1. Submit task: kspec task submit @task\\n  2. Create PR: /pr skill\\n  3. Stop responding — ralph handles PR review via separate subagent\\n\",\n      \"execution\": {\n        \"mode\": \"silent\"\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"_sourceFile\": \"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/.kspec/kynetic.meta.yaml\"\n}\n","status":"completed"}